WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.440
- Do you know what it feels
like to be 26 years old,

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.930
have people that you
went to high school with

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:06.500
come to your liquor store,

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.300
look you dead in the
face as they pulled up

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.217
in their BMW and say,

00:00:10.217 --> 00:00:12.840
"Oh, you work for your dad?"

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.140
And then you ring them up
on their case of champagne

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.030
and you bring it out
to their car and put it

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.970
in their trunk and they look
you in the face with pity?

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.090
I lived that life.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.067
And the way I took that scene was,

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.117
"I'll see you in 10 years, motherfucker!"

00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:28.367
(energetic rock music)

00:00:33.565 --> 00:00:36.315
(dramatic music)

00:00:42.747 --> 00:00:43.580
You know, it's funnier.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.560
I was driving here this morning,

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.177
I was like, "What do I want to get off?

00:00:47.177 --> 00:00:48.950
"What do I want to make sure they know."

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.680
The number one thing if
I leave this morning,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.250
that I hope, is for people to realize

00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:56.320
how much leverage they have.

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:00.000
How you, just like weight room and film,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.440
you got to put in work
to get what you want

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:04.970
and how, what social
media and the internet

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.760
have done has given
you so much opportunity

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:09.880
to take advantage of who you engage with

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:11.490
around what you want.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.630
I think the biggest
vulnerability to this room,

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:17.810
including the coaches, and
us old guys is patience.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:21.720
I wish, the coaches over here,
knew how young they were.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.690
Watching 30, 40, 50 year-olds

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:26.580
completely confused by
the context of time,

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.340
is one of the most fascinating
things I see in our society.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.087
Like, people always come
up to me and they're like,

00:01:31.087 --> 00:01:32.630
"Gary, when are you
going to buy the Jets?"

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.280
and I'm like, "25 years,"
and they get sad as fuck.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.400
Like, they think I, they like
want me to have it tomorrow.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.430
There was a really famous
basketball college team,

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:42.450
Loyola Marymount.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:44.570
Every time I think about that team,

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:45.950
it's how I think about my life

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.240
and how I think about
myself as an entrepreneur.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.370
They will win college basketball games

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.433
like 147 to 132.

00:01:53.430 --> 00:01:54.500
They would just run and shoot.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.430
They were just, (exhales)
they just pushed it.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:00.570
Their games were crazy and
that's how I think about life.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.130
I think too many people
are playing defense.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.533
And I'm out here trying to win 149 to 146.

00:02:06.533 --> 00:02:07.620
Offense.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.830
Because once you stop hearing judgment,

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.380
and you're not actually worried about

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:13.960
what people have to say,
you can just go fast.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.150
Judgment is the only thing I promise you

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.033
that you'll have for
the rest of your life.

00:02:19.364 --> 00:02:22.531
(upbeat trance music)

